{
  "requirement": "requirements.ci.errors",
  "file": "src/evidence.rs",
  "item": "fn[reference_set_digest_for]",
  "queries": [
    "early_exits",
    "error_accumulators"
  ],
  "applies": false,
  "fixmes": [],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.ci.errors` does not apply to `reference_set_digest_for` (src/evidence.rs:1262-1297).\n\n- **Scope of the requirement.** The sites clause covers \"a repository-validation function that collects validation errors\". It says \"authoring code that collects errors only to abort is not one.\"\n- **What this function does.** It is a helper that computes the reference-set digest of one requirement or example. Its callers are authoring code and test fixtures that stamp or compare the `references` field. The repository validator (`validate_repository`) is a separate function.\n- **How it uses `errors`.**\n  - The first `errors` vector gathers problems from `book_source_dir` and `collect_definitions`, and the function never reads it. The comment in the code says those problems \"do not change this definition's reference set\".\n  - The second `errors` vector gathers problems from `discovered_files` and `collect_references_with_progress`. The function returns `Err(io::Error::other(...))` if it is non-empty. That is collecting errors only to abort.\n- **Why the `errors` variable does not make it a site.** The `error_accumulators` query matches the function only because it has a local named `errors`. The requirement's prose excludes this kind of code.\n\nThe listed violation matches therefore do not break the requirement here:\n- `fs::canonicalize(root)?` (line 1266),\n- the `.ok_or_else(...)?` on the definition lookup (lines 1272-1280),\n- `return Err(...)` (line 1285),\n- `definition_sites(...)?` (line 1288).\n\nEach one is an abort in code that is not a validation sequencer. I found no gap.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "file": "src/evidence.rs",
      "item": "fn[reference_set_digest_for]",
      "hash": "64b21ac7f69b5b8c3d957e7e4969a454e60552fc837f7fcb19ed965b97164dab"
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.ci.errors",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.ci.errors"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::::{req} errors",
        "Repository validation MUST continue after a failed check and report every failed",
        "check it finds in one run, each as a {term}`requirements.ci.validation_error`.",
        "This is a convention for every validation error; the requirement for each check",
        "states which conditions that check reports. A file that cannot be parsed, such as",
        "a malformed `habeas.toml`, `book.toml`, or evidence file, is one failed check:",
        "its error MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem in that file, and",
        "checks that do not depend on its contents MUST still run.",
        "",
        "The code that sequences the repository's checks carries out the first paragraph.",
        "A repository-validation function that collects validation errors MUST hold them",
        "in a parameter or local variable named `errors`, and a function with such a",
        "variable is a site below; authoring code that collects errors only to abort is",
        "not one. After one of its checks fails, a site MUST still run every later check",
        "that does not depend on the failed check's result, including later checks in the",
        "same loop iteration, and MUST NOT report one failure twice.",
        "",
        "::::{sites} error_accumulators",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src]",
        "exclude: [src/authoring/inputs.rs, src/authoring/tools.rs]",
        "rule:",
        "  kind: function_item",
        "  has:",
        "    stopBy: { kind: function_item }",
        "    any:",
        "      - kind: parameter",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "      - kind: let_declaration",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "  not:",
        "    inside:",
        "      stopBy: end",
        "      kind: mod_item",
        "      has: { field: name, regex: \"^tests$\" }",
        "match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut errors: BTreeSet<String> = BTreeSet::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut errors);",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, discovery_errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut problems = Vec::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut problems);",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    mod tests {",
        "        fn check(errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        "",
        "::::{violations} early_exits",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src]",
        "within: error_accumulators",
        "rule:",
        "  any:",
        "    - kind: try_expression",
        "    - kind: return_expression",
        "    - kind: continue_expression",
        "    - kind: break_expression",
        "match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); continue; }",
        "            if item.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        if !v.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); return; }",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); break; }",
        "        }",
        "        if items.is_empty() { errors.push(\"empty\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn parse(v: &Value) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        ":::::"
      ]
    },
